# A B1.9 buttress thread with its roots rounded: the chord tolerance set
# fine enough in the preferences, the designation typed with the load's
# way, PULL-BUTT, which ticks the load flank turned back, and the rounded
# root ticked at the end of the crest's row; then made.
key c
move 300 300
down L 300 300
up L 300 300
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
key esc
key x shift
key esc
menu Edit|Preferences...
# [change] the chord tolerance to 0.02%.
twmove 110 295
twdown L 110 295
twup L 110 295
edit 0.02
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
menu Features|Screw Thread...
twmove 172 110
twdown L 172 110
twup L 172 110
edit 1/2-16 PULL-BUTT
tw
# The rounded root, at the end of the crest's row.
twmove 690 190
twdown L 690 190
twup L 690 190
tw
# Flip the direction, down into the part; then made.
twmove 60 230
twdown L 60 230
twup L 60 230
twmove 37 260
twdown L 37 260
twup L 37 260
tw
dump
